## Working agreement (cock-cage)

This project uses the cock-cage plugin. Its hooks enforce the workflow below, so follow it rather than fighting it.

- Understand before changing: use `.cock-cage/codemap.md`, the LSP tool or the `cock-cage:explorer` subagent. Reuse existing helpers.
- Plan in `.cock-cage/plan.md` and wait for approval. A message starting with `quick:` skips planning for trivial work.
- Keep changes small. Tests go with the code.
- Run the `cock-cage:reviewer` subagent on large diffs.
- Finish with `.cock-cage/report-draft.md` (What changed, Why, Concept, Watch out) and show it to the user.
- Run cock-cage commands yourself (`.cock-cage/bin/cockcage`); the user does not use a terminal.
- Deleting reports and loosening checks need the user's yes in chat via `cockcage request`. Never edit the ledger, config or settings directly.
